Added `pas.plugins.identity` as an always installed dependency, with `Person` as the user content type: each user account is a `Person` in the new `/users` folder, while other `Person` objects stay plain content. An upgrade step installs the add-on on existing sites and creates a `Person` for each user in `source_users`. Site creation gains the `identity-keycloak`, `identity-oidc`, `identity-github` and `identity-google` authentication providers, configured with `identity-*` answers or `SITE_AUTHENTICATION_IDENTITY-*` environment variables. With `identity-keycloak`, the realm groups come from `pas.plugins.keycloakgroups`, and Keycloak users get their Keycloak user id (`sub`) as Plone userid. @ericof
